.\" Manpage for sread
.TH sread 1 "2026-05-13" "sread 1.0" "Terminal sleep read"
.SH NAME
sread \- terminal sleep read
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sread
.RI "-t" " <time-in-seconds>"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sread
\(lq sleep read \(rq\) is a small C program that waits for a single keypress
without requiring the Enter key. When a key is pressed, \fBsread\fP writes that
key to stdout and ends the sleep early. If no key is pressed within the
specified time, \fBsread\fP exits after the timeout.

\fBsread\fP behaves like the standard \fBsleep\fP command, but it allows the
sleep to be interrupted by a single keypress and returns that key on stdout.
Fractional seconds are supported, for example:
.PP
.EX
sread -t 1.22
.EE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h
Show a short usage message.
.TP
.B -t time
Time to sleep in seconds; fractional values are allowed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
while true
do
  url=$(selectmusicstream)
  duration=$(send_to_upnp_speaker "${url}")
  key=$(sread -t "${duration}")

  if [ "${key}" = "q" ]; then break; fi
  if [ "${key}" = "+" ]; then incvolume; fi
  if [ "${key}" = "-" ]; then decvolume; fi
done
.EE
.SH BUGS
Unknown; probably.
